## Wisp
- Wisp
- Infrared Imaging  SENSOR
- Wisp delivers passive infrared detection & tracking to enable persistent hemispheric situational awareness at long ranges for a variety of domains and mission sets.
- Wisp:
- ![Wisp passive infrared sensor with 360-degree horizontal and 125-degree vertical field of view for detecting dismounts, vehicles, UAS, and aircraft at long range, shown in product view](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/61nocsj5/production/38d5d6735fa342cd9c1ba96fa43cf6b2f5d7a704-4000x2659.png?rect=905,358,2014,2118&w=1000&fit=min&auto=format)
  - Automated Detection Range: Dismount (5 km); Vehicles (15 km); UAS (20 km); Commercial Aircraft (150 km)
  - Sensor Field of View:  360° Horizontal; 125° Vertical
  - Form Factor : Sensor (15" x 15" x 22"); Processor (19" x 8" x 26")
- TAKE CONTROL
- Build Qualities
- Passive: Wisp emits no signal and cannot be jammed, enabling radar-like detecting without detection.
- Adaptable: Wisp operates on multiple platforms and across domains for missions including base protection, counter drone, and maritime security.
  - ![Wisp sensor deployed atop a military boat across multiple platforms including fixed site, vehicle, and maritime configurations for diverse mission applications](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/61nocsj5/production/a450f330f9bdc4ace0f4de2355c1483267e640f0-1202x800.png?w=1000&fit=min&auto=format)
- Interoperable: Open architecture enables integration into any GOTS/COTS C2 or sensor system.
- Persistent: Provides a single operator with always-on, alarm-based security against 360-degree ground and airborne threats.
  - ![Wisp sensor backlit with sunlight in a field, providing a single operator with always-on 360-degree alarm-based persistent surveillance against ground and airborne threats](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/61nocsj5/production/3eb9b703052c99dfebf952d2c3ab8248ddbdbac5-3000x2250.jpg?w=1000&fit=min&auto=format)
